Source URL: https://www.snopes.com/fact-check/trump-revolutionary-war-airports/

### During what specific speech, interview, or public appearance did Donald Trump make the statement about airports in the Revolutionary War?
Answer: Donald Trump made the statement about airports in the Revolutionary War during his Independence Day speech on July 4, 2019, in Washington, D.C.

Source URL: https://www.snopes.com/fact-check/trump-revolutionary-war-airports/

### Have reputable news organizations or historians verified that Donald Trump made a factual error by claiming airports existed during the Revolutionary War?
Answer: Yes, reputable fact-checking organizations like Snopes have verified that Donald Trump made a factual error by claiming airports existed during the Revolutionary War. As reported, during his 2019 Independence Day speech, Trump stated, "Our army manned the air, it rammed the ramparts, it took over the airports," which is anachronistic since "no airports existed in the 18th century (the first successful airplane wasn't flown until 1903)."

Source URL: https://www.snopes.com/fact-check/trump-revolutionary-war-airports/

